WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:07.580
Why does bond formation take place?

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.960
Can you give me the answer?

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.660
Yes, it takes place

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:14.820
because atoms are always in a constant struggle

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:17.140
to reach the stable state.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.560
And what is this stable state?

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:22.220
Well, if the atoms have only one shell,

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:24.160
then the stable state is achieved

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:27.220
when two electrons are present in it.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:30.360
And if the atom has two or more than two shells

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:32.140
then the stable state is achieved

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:35.820
when the outermost shell contains eight electrons.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:37.680
It's called an octet.

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:42.020
But the stable state is seen only in case of a few elements.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:46.320
We know that elements like Helium, Neon, Argon etc

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:50.460
have atoms with such desired electronic configuration.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:54.600
But what about the case of atoms which do not have this octet?

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:58.500
Yes, they will participate in bond formation.

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:03.060
That means they will either give or take or share electrons.

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:06.240
But wait, who decides how many electrons

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:08.720
will participate in the bond formation?

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:13.220
Or who tells the atoms if they've to give or take electrons?

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:17.160
Well, the answer to these questions is valency.

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:20.120
Let's understand this concept in detail.

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:21.540
In simple words,

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:25.880
valency is defined as the combining capacity of an element.

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:28.440
Now what exactly do we mean by this?

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:30.800
When we say combining capacity,

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:35.180
that means how much can an atom bond with another atom.

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:37.660
Does that mean how many electrons can be given

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:40.100
or taken or even shared?

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:41.280
Yes!

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:43.940
Thus, the capacity of an atom to give electrons,

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:46.640
accept electrons or even share them

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:48.900
in order to achieve the octet state,

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:51.600
can be termed as its valency.

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:55.200
And what about the case of elements with just one shell?

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:56.580
That's correct!

00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:58.680
Trading of electrons is carried out

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:01.200
for attaining two electrons in the outermost

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:04.580
and only orbital in such atoms.

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:07.680
Let us take simple examples to understand this.

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:12.600
In case of Hydrogen, we have just one electron in the outermost shell.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:15.060
That means, it has to somehow add

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:18.700
one more electron to the outermost shell.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:21.860
Thus we find that the valency of Hydrogen is one

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:22.900
as it accepts

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:27.460
or sometimes even shares electrons with atoms of other elements.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:30.960
So can you tell me the valency of Oxygen now?

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:35.020
The electronic configuration of Oxygen is 2,6.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:38.920
That means it has 6 electrons in the outermost shell.

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:42.640
So how many electrons are needed to complete the octet?

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:45.400
Yes, 2 electrons.

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:48.380
Thus the valency of Oxygen is 2.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:51.980
It accepts or takes 2 electrons from other atoms

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:53.700
for completing the octet.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:57.720
Now tell me what will be the valency of Magnesium?

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:00.880
We know that Magnesium has 12 electrons.

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:06.420
That means the electronic configuration of Magnesium is 2, 8, 2.

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:09.140
So how many electrons will be needed now?

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:11.440
6, that's correct!

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:13.660
And that's what we're able to see.

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:16.700
6 electrons are needed to complete the octet.

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:20.480
But which atom will give away 6 electrons so easily?

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:22.280
Is it even possible?

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:23.420
Not really!

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:26.660
Then how will Magnesium complete its octet?

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:28.020
This is where the concept

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:30.860
of donating electrons comes into the picture.

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:34.280
If managing the gain of 6 electrons is difficult,

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:37.960
then can it think of giving or donating the 2 electrons?

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:39.860
Yes, absolutely!

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:43.920
So if Magnesium gives away 2 electrons from its outermost shell,

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:47.320
then we say that the valency of Magnesium is 2.

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:51.480
That means it's not only about how many electrons can be taken,

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:56.100
but also about how many electrons can be given by the atom.

00:03:56.260 --> 00:04:00.320
That is how we calculate the valencies of various elements.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.700
Now to understand the concept better,

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:05.980
let's take an example of elements forming one compound.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:09.060
May be we can think of Sodium chloride.

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:11.460
For the formation of one molecule,

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:15.600
we need one atom of Sodium and one atom of Chlorine.

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:18.720
What are the valencies of each by the way?

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:22.520
Sodium has the electronic configuration 2, 8, 1.

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:27.360
While Chlorine as an electronic configuration 2, 8, 7.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.560
Before I tell you what happens,

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:31.760
I want you to give it a shot.

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:33.840
What do you think will happen?

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:37.060
Doesn't this indicate that Sodium will donate one

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:39.580
and Chlorine will accept one electron

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:42.180
to complete their respective octet state?

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:44.700
Yes, that's absolutely correct!

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:49.000
And that is what helps in the formation of Sodium chloride molecule.

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:52.500
Chlorine needed one electron which it got from Sodium.

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:54.560
And Sodium gave one electron,

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:58.620
as it was the easiest way to achieve stability.

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:03.120
So the valency of both Sodium and Chlorine is 1.

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:06.300
Does this mean that only elements having the same valency

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:08.800
always combined together to form a bond?

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:10.260
Not really!

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:13.700
Just take the simple example of a water molecule.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.840
We have seen that the valency of Hydrogen is 1

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:19.140
while that of Oxygen is 2.

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:21.860
Here, Hydrogen needs 1 electron,

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:24.440
while Oxygen needs two electrons.

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:26.580
Both need electrons.

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:29.800
So how do the atoms combine in this case?

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:32.660
How will the bond formation take place then?

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:36.640
Well, they will both share electrons with each other.

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:38.100
But how?

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:40.040
It's not that straight forward.

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:43.280
We will understand it in one of our future videos.

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:46.820
For now, we have to know that one atom of Oxygen

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:51.440
combines with two Hydrogen atoms to give us one water molecule.

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:54.700
This is how atoms with different valencies

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:57.740
combine with each other to form compounds.

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:01.360
Now that we know how the concept of valency works,

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:03.760
let's have a look at how the atoms come together

00:06:03.940 --> 00:06:06.260
to form independent units.

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:11.100
Let's discuss the concept of molecules in the next video.

